{
  "about": "Curved text (row 74): the `curve` text param (-100 to 100) bends the flat text raster along a circular arc; at 100 the raster's width wraps 350 degrees. radius = width / angle. Positive is an arch (the circle's centre below the text, the ends drop), negative a smile. `points` are flat points (pixels from the raster's centre, y down) and where they land; `sizes` the bent raster's size, centred on the flat raster's centre (2 x (ceil(reach) + 1), parts past the circle's centre left out). Checked by crates/textwarp (and the web through WASM). Expected values from an independent Python reference (rotation matrices, dense sampling).",
